{"jurisdiction":"NE","generatedAt":"2026-11-05T05:54:04Z","bills":{"NE-2025-LR478":{"id":"NE-2025-LR478","passed":false,"number":"LR 478","title":"Interim study to examine the governance and operational structure of Nebraska's prescription drug monitoring program, including its relationship with the health information exchange","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-03-25","sponsor":{"name":"Ballard","party":"Nonpartisan","state":"NE","district":"21"},"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-10-09","text":"Notice of hearing for November 16, 2026","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-30","text":"Referred to Health and Human Services Committee","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-25","text":"Referred to Executive Board","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-25","text":"Date of introduction","chamber":"Legislature"}],"law":null,"policyArea":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/bills/search_by_date.php?SessionDay=2026","textUrl":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR478.pdf","versions":[{"label":"Introduced","date":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR478.pdf","type":"PDF"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The resolution would assign the Health and Human Services Committee to study how Nebraska’s prescription drug monitoring program is run and operated, including how it works with the health information exchange. After the study, the committee would report its findings and recommendations to the Legislature or the Legislative Council.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"NE-2025-LR380":{"id":"NE-2025-LR380","passed":false,"number":"LR 380","title":"Interim study to identify the needs of youth moving and transitioning to and from a youth rehabilitation and treatment center, an adult correctional facility, or a residential treatment facility as proposed by LB867","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-03-20","sponsor":{"name":"Fredrickson","party":"Nonpartisan","state":"NE","district":"20"},"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-10-05","text":"Notice of hearing for November 16, 2026","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-30","text":"Referred to Health and Human Services Committee","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-20","text":"Referred to Executive Board","chamber":"Legislature"},{"date":"2026-03-20","text":"Date of introduction","chamber":"Legislature"}],"law":null,"policyArea":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/bills/search_by_date.php?SessionDay=2026","textUrl":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR380.pdf","versions":[{"label":"Introduced","date":null,"url":"https://nebraskalegislature.gov/FloorDocs/109/PDF/Intro/LR380.pdf","type":"PDF"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"This resolution would direct a legislative committee to study the needs of youth moving to and from a youth rehabilitation and treatment center, an adult correctional facility, or a residential treatment facility. The study would look at current placement plans, the needs of the youth and their families, other possible facility models, and any law or policy changes needed to carry out a plan based on evidence. The committee would report its findings and recommendations after the study ends.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"NE-2025-LR415":{"id":"NE-2025-LR415","passed":false,"number":"LR 415","title":"Interim study to examine current practices under Nebraska law related to the designation of real property as blighted and substandard","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-03-24","sponsor":{"name":"Conrad","party":"Nonpartisan","state":"NE","district":"46"},"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":